  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nThe long term forecast period will be characterized by a welcomed\npattern change. An upper level trough digs down across the Midwest\ntowards the Southeast during the middle of the week. This will push \na cold front through the area Tuesday night through Wednesday and as \na result, low to medium chances (30-50%) for showers and storms \nare expected through Tuesday night.\n\nAs the upper level trough axis shifts to our east, northwest flow\nbegins to advect in a noticeably cooler and drier airmass \nbringing some much needed relief from the heat. We begin to really\nfeel the drier air late Wednesday night into Thursday as \ndewpoints fall into the lower 60s. Afternoon highs Thursday \nthrough Saturday are forecast to only rise into the low to mid 80s\nwith overnight lows in the upper 50s to lower 60s.",
